    "summary": "Wooden mask in the form of a flatfish, mounted on a wooden ring with wooden pegs tied to the ring with sinew. Also pegged with the fish are four flippers and two fish; a traingular piece of wood at the tail and a feather above the head carved on the back of the fish. a face of a seal or Tunghak (keeper of the game (represented by a mustache)) is carved and painted in the centre of halibut. Mask painted white, blue and red. Unused.",
